00:05:08,571 --> 00:05:14,571
Power changes everything

2
00:10:17,142 --> 00:10:23,142
The Current War is a drama, history film directed by Alfonso Gomez-Rejon.

3
00:15:25,714 --> 00:15:31,714
Electricity titans Thomas Edison and George Westinghouse compete to create
a sustainable system and market it to the American people.

4
00:20:34,285 --> 00:20:40,285
Thomas Edison, played by Benedict Cumberbatch.

5
00:25:42,857 --> 00:25:48,857
George Westinghouse, played by Michael Shannon.

6
00:30:51,428 --> 00:30:57,428
Nikola Tesla, played by Nicholas Hoult.

7
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Marguerite Westinghouse, played by Katherine Waterston.

8
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:14,571
Samuel Insull, played by Tom Holland.

9
00:46:17,142 --> 00:46:23,142
J.P. Morgan, played by Matthew Macfadyen.

10
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
The Current War is a 2017 historical drama film inspired by the 19th-century competition between Thomas Edison and George Westinghouse over
which electric power delivery system would be used in the United States (often referred to as the "war of the currents").

11
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
Directed by Alfonso Gomez-Rejon, written by Michael Mitnick, and executive produced by Martin Scorsese and Steven Zaillian, the film stars Benedict Cumberbatch as Edison, Michael Shannon
as Westinghouse, Nicholas Hoult as Nikola Tesla, and Tom Holland as Samuel Insull, alongside Katherine Waterston, Tuppence Middleton, Matthew Macfadyen and Damien Molony.

12
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
Announced in May 2012, Gomez-Rejon was confirmed in September 2015.

13
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
Cumberbatch, Shannon, and Hoult joined the cast by October
2016, and filming began in England that December.

14
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film premiered at the Toronto International
Film Festival on September 9, 2017.

15
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
Originally to be distributed by The Weinstein Company, the film was shelved and sold in
November 2017 following the sexual abuse allegations made against Harvey Weinstein.

16
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
It was eventually bought by Weinstein Company successor Lantern Entertainment,
which then sold domestic distribution rights to 101 Studios.

17
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
After discovering a final cut privilege clause in Scorsese's contract, Gomez-Rejon convinced him to allow for reshoots and to trim
ten minutes off the original version's runtime, resulting in the film that was eventually released into theaters.

18
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
The film was released in the United States on October 25, 2019.

19
01:37:42,857 --> 01:37:48,857
The film received generally mixed reviews, with praise towards the cast's performances and
the intriguing story, but with criticism towards the overall execution.

20
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
The tone is emotional.
